{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Your server speaks AG-UI. TanStack "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat"},{"type":"text","value":" still misses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"finishReason"},{"type":"text","value":", the model id, or leftover usage. Put those extras in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata.tanstack"},{"type":"text","value":" on the event. Spec fields stay at the top."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Copy this "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_FINISHED"},{"type":"text","value":" event first:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"{\n  \"type\": \"RUN_FINISHED\",\n  \"threadId\": \"thread-1\",\n  \"runId\": \"run-1\",\n  \"usage\": [\n    {\n      \"inputTokens\": 12,\n      \"outputTokens\": 34,\n      \"totalTokens\": 46\n    }\n  ],\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"tanstack\": {\n      \"finishReason\": \"stop\",\n      \"model\": \"gpt-5.5\"\n    }\n  }\n}","lang":"json"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The client copies "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata.tanstack"},{"type":"text","value":" onto the chunk. After "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chunk.type === \"RUN_FINISHED\""},{"type":"text","value":", read "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chunk.metadata?.tanstack?.finishReason"},{"type":"text","value":". In-process "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"usage"},{"type":"text","value":" is TanStack "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TokenUsage"},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"promptTokens"},{"type":"text","value":"). The wire uses the spec array ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"inputTokens"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"do-now","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Do now"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Send these on every successful run:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Field"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Where"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why the client needs it"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"type"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"threadId"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runId"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Spec top level"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Frame the run. Missing ids break resume and correlation."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"usage[]"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Spec top level on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_FINISHED"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_ERROR"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Token counts. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"inputTokens"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"outputTokens"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"totalTokens"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"finishReason"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata.tanstack"},{"type":"text","value":" on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_FINISHED"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After a tool result, the client continues only when this is not "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"stop\""},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"model"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata.tanstack"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SSE "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[DONE]"},{"type":"text","value":" fallback and generation reconstruct."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"finishReason"},{"type":"text","value":" is one of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"stop\""},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"length\""},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"content_filter\""},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"tool_calls\""},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you omit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"finishReason"},{"type":"text","value":" after a tool result, the client treats it as not "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"stop\""},{"type":"text","value":" and can send another turn."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"read-it-on-the-client","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read it on the client"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\n\nconst { messages } = useChat({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  onChunk: (chunk) => {\n    if (chunk.type === \"RUN_FINISHED\") {\n      console.log(chunk.usage);\n      console.log(chunk.metadata?.tanstack?.finishReason);\n      console.log(chunk.metadata?.tanstack?.model);\n    }\n  },\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Do not import a helper. Check "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chunk.type"},{"type":"text","value":", then read "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chunk.metadata?.tanstack"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"run-error","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_ERROR"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"AG-UI "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_ERROR"},{"type":"text","value":" has "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"message"},{"type":"text","value":" and optional "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"code"},{"type":"text","value":" at the top. Put correlation ids in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata.tanstack"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"{\n  \"type\": \"RUN_ERROR\",\n  \"message\": \"Provider timeout\",\n  \"code\": \"TIMEOUT\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"tanstack\": {\n      \"threadId\": \"thread-1\",\n      \"runId\": \"run-1\",\n      \"model\": \"gpt-5.5\"\n    }\n  }\n}","lang":"json"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"later","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Later"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add these when you use the matching feature:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Leftover usage."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Spec "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"usage[]"},{"type":"text","value":" also accepts "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cachedInputTokens"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reasoningTokens"},{"type":"text","value":". Put "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cost"},{"type":"text","value":" and other leftover fields in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata.tanstack.usage"},{"type":"text","value":". The client rebuilds TanStack "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TokenUsage"},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"promptTokens"},{"type":"text","value":") from the array plus that leftover."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interrupt errors."}]},{"type":"text","value":" On "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_ERROR"},{"type":"text","value":", set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata.tanstack.interruptErrors"},{"type":"text","value":" so "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChatClient"},{"type":"text","value":" can match a failed interrupt submit."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tool output error."}]},{"type":"text","value":" On "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TOOL_CALL_RESULT"},{"type":"text","value":", set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata.tanstack.state"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"output-error\""},{"type":"text","value":" when the tool result is an error payload."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Message stamps."}]},{"type":"text","value":" On wire messages, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata.tanstack.createdAt"},{"type":"text","value":" is an ISO-8601 string."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Signatures."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Stream thinking signatures on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"REASONING_ENCRYPTED_VALUE"},{"type":"text","value":". On the next-turn body, set spec "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"encryptedValue"},{"type":"text","value":" on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"role: \"reasoning\""},{"type":"text","value":" messages and on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolCalls"},{"type":"text","value":". Other tool-call provider fields stay in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata.tanstack.toolCallMetadata"},{"type":"text","value":". See "},{"type":"link","href":"../chat/thinking-content","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Thinking & Reasoning"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A TanStack "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" server already writes this bag. Use this page when you emit AG-UI events yourself."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"../chat/stream-events","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stream Events"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the event table, and "},{"type":"link","href":"../migration/ag-ui-compliance","children":[{"type":"text","value":"AG-UI Client Compliance"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the request body."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"do-now","text":"Do now","level":2},{"id":"read-it-on-the-client","text":"Read it on the client","level":2},{"id":"run-error","text":"RUN_ERROR","level":2},{"id":"later","text":"Later","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nYour server speaks AG-UI. TanStack `useChat` still misses `finishReason`, the model id, or leftover usage. Put those extras in `metadata.tanstack` on the event. Spec fields stay at the top.\n\nCopy this `RUN_FINISHED` event first:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"RUN_FINISHED\",\n  \"threadId\": \"thread-1\",\n  \"runId\": \"run-1\",\n  \"usage\": [\n    {\n      \"inputTokens\": 12,\n      \"outputTokens\": 34,\n      \"totalTokens\": 46\n    }\n  ],\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"tanstack\": {\n      \"finishReason\": \"stop\",\n      \"model\": \"gpt-5.5\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe client copies `metadata.tanstack` onto the chunk. After `chunk.type === \"RUN_FINISHED\"`, read `chunk.metadata?.tanstack?.finishReason`. In-process `usage` is TanStack `TokenUsage` (`promptTokens`). The wire uses the spec array (`inputTokens`).\n\n## Do now\n\nSend these on every successful run:\n\n| Field | Where | Why the client needs it |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `type`, `threadId`, `runId` | Spec top level | Frame the run. Missing ids break resume and correlation. |\n| `usage[]` | Spec top level on `RUN_FINISHED` / `RUN_ERROR` | Token counts. Use `inputTokens`, `outputTokens`, `totalTokens`. |\n| `finishReason` | `metadata.tanstack` on `RUN_FINISHED` | After a tool result, the client continues only when this is not `\"stop\"`. |\n| `model` | `metadata.tanstack` | SSE `[DONE]` fallback and generation reconstruct. |\n\n`finishReason` is one of `\"stop\"`, `\"length\"`, `\"content_filter\"`, `\"tool_calls\"`, or `null`.\n\nIf you omit `finishReason` after a tool result, the client treats it as not `\"stop\"` and can send another turn.\n\n## Read it on the client\n\n```typescript\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\n\nconst { messages } = useChat({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  onChunk: (chunk) => {\n    if (chunk.type === \"RUN_FINISHED\") {\n      console.log(chunk.usage);\n      console.log(chunk.metadata?.tanstack?.finishReason);\n      console.log(chunk.metadata?.tanstack?.model);\n    }\n  },\n});\n```\n\nDo not import a helper. Check `chunk.type`, then read `chunk.metadata?.tanstack`.\n\n## `RUN_ERROR`\n\nAG-UI `RUN_ERROR` has `message` and optional `code` at the top. Put correlation ids in `metadata.tanstack`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"RUN_ERROR\",\n  \"message\": \"Provider timeout\",\n  \"code\": \"TIMEOUT\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"tanstack\": {\n      \"threadId\": \"thread-1\",\n      \"runId\": \"run-1\",\n      \"model\": \"gpt-5.5\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Later\n\nAdd these when you use the matching feature:\n\n- **Leftover usage.** Spec `usage[]` also accepts `cachedInputTokens` and `reasoningTokens`. Put `cost` and other leftover fields in `metadata.tanstack.usage`. The client rebuilds TanStack `TokenUsage` (`promptTokens`) from the array plus that leftover.\n- **Interrupt errors.** On `RUN_ERROR`, set `metadata.tanstack.interruptErrors` so `ChatClient` can match a failed interrupt submit.\n- **Tool output error.** On `TOOL_CALL_RESULT`, set `metadata.tanstack.state` to `\"output-error\"` when the tool result is an error payload.\n- **Message stamps.** On wire messages, `metadata.tanstack.createdAt` is an ISO-8601 string.\n- **Signatures.** Stream thinking signatures on `REASONING_ENCRYPTED_VALUE`. On the next-turn body, set spec `encryptedValue` on `role: \"reasoning\"` messages and on `toolCalls`. Other tool-call provider fields stay in `metadata.tanstack.toolCallMetadata`. See [Thinking & Reasoning](../chat/thinking-content).\n\nA TanStack `chat()` server already writes this bag. Use this page when you emit AG-UI events yourself.\n\nSee [Stream Events](../chat/stream-events) for the event table, and [AG-UI Client Compliance](../migration/ag-ui-compliance) for the request body.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Event metadata\nid: protocol-event-metadata\norder: 1\ndescription: \"What a custom AG-UI server must put in metadata.tanstack so TanStack ChatClient and useChat get finishReason, model, and leftover usage.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - ag-ui protocol\n  - metadata.tanstack\n  - finishReason\n  - custom server\n  - SSE\n---\n\nYour server speaks AG-UI. TanStack `useChat` still misses `finishReason`, the model id, or leftover usage. Put those extras in `metadata.tanstack` on the event. Spec fields stay at the top.\n\nCopy this `RUN_FINISHED` event first:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"RUN_FINISHED\",\n  \"threadId\": \"thread-1\",\n  \"runId\": \"run-1\",\n  \"usage\": [\n    {\n      \"inputTokens\": 12,\n      \"outputTokens\": 34,\n      \"totalTokens\": 46\n    }\n  ],\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"tanstack\": {\n      \"finishReason\": \"stop\",\n      \"model\": \"gpt-5.5\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe client copies `metadata.tanstack` onto the chunk. After `chunk.type === \"RUN_FINISHED\"`, read `chunk.metadata?.tanstack?.finishReason`. In-process `usage` is TanStack `TokenUsage` (`promptTokens`). The wire uses the spec array (`inputTokens`).\n\n## Do now\n\nSend these on every successful run:\n\n| Field | Where | Why the client needs it |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `type`, `threadId`, `runId` | Spec top level | Frame the run. Missing ids break resume and correlation. |\n| `usage[]` | Spec top level on `RUN_FINISHED` / `RUN_ERROR` | Token counts. Use `inputTokens`, `outputTokens`, `totalTokens`. |\n| `finishReason` | `metadata.tanstack` on `RUN_FINISHED` | After a tool result, the client continues only when this is not `\"stop\"`. |\n| `model` | `metadata.tanstack` | SSE `[DONE]` fallback and generation reconstruct. |\n\n`finishReason` is one of `\"stop\"`, `\"length\"`, `\"content_filter\"`, `\"tool_calls\"`, or `null`.\n\nIf you omit `finishReason` after a tool result, the client treats it as not `\"stop\"` and can send another turn.\n\n## Read it on the client\n\n```typescript\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\n\nconst { messages } = useChat({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  onChunk: (chunk) => {\n    if (chunk.type === \"RUN_FINISHED\") {\n      console.log(chunk.usage);\n      console.log(chunk.metadata?.tanstack?.finishReason);\n      console.log(chunk.metadata?.tanstack?.model);\n    }\n  },\n});\n```\n\nDo not import a helper. Check `chunk.type`, then read `chunk.metadata?.tanstack`.\n\n## `RUN_ERROR`\n\nAG-UI `RUN_ERROR` has `message` and optional `code` at the top. Put correlation ids in `metadata.tanstack`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"RUN_ERROR\",\n  \"message\": \"Provider timeout\",\n  \"code\": \"TIMEOUT\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"tanstack\": {\n      \"threadId\": \"thread-1\",\n      \"runId\": \"run-1\",\n      \"model\": \"gpt-5.5\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Later\n\nAdd these when you use the matching feature:\n\n- **Leftover usage.** Spec `usage[]` also accepts `cachedInputTokens` and `reasoningTokens`. Put `cost` and other leftover fields in `metadata.tanstack.usage`. The client rebuilds TanStack `TokenUsage` (`promptTokens`) from the array plus that leftover.\n- **Interrupt errors.** On `RUN_ERROR`, set `metadata.tanstack.interruptErrors` so `ChatClient` can match a failed interrupt submit.\n- **Tool output error.** On `TOOL_CALL_RESULT`, set `metadata.tanstack.state` to `\"output-error\"` when the tool result is an error payload.\n- **Message stamps.** On wire messages, `metadata.tanstack.createdAt` is an ISO-8601 string.\n- **Signatures.** Stream thinking signatures on `REASONING_ENCRYPTED_VALUE`. On the next-turn body, set spec `encryptedValue` on `role: \"reasoning\"` messages and on `toolCalls`. Other tool-call provider fields stay in `metadata.tanstack.toolCallMetadata`. See [Thinking & Reasoning](../chat/thinking-content).\n\nA TanStack `chat()` server already writes this bag. Use this page when you emit AG-UI events yourself.\n\nSee [Stream Events](../chat/stream-events) for the event table, and [AG-UI Client Compliance](../migration/ag-ui-compliance) for the request body.\n"}
